      "writtenOn": "2024-04-09T17:34:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There were performance regressions in ganesh when I tried to make it go to 0.50001 before the approx-fit work that\u0027s gone into avoiding it in image filtering.\n\nIf we do exactly 0.5, it\u0027s possible for linear filtering to select the subset edge pixel with a weight of 1.0 and an outside pixel with a weight of 0. Visually it shouldn\u0027t matter, but it makes MSAN mad and some GPUs don\u0027t quite get the weights right. Clamping to a slightly more than 1/2px makes sure the weight goes from an inside pixel to an edge pixel.",
      "parentUuid": "26210d23_929cee62",
